  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "P = Q_n^{*n} \\quad \\text{(n-fold convolution of } Q_n \\text{ with itself)}",
    "plain": "A distribution is infinitely divisible if it can be split into arbitrarily many identical independent pieces. The Gaussian, Poisson, Cauchy, and Gamma distributions are all infinitely divisible. The Lévy-Khintchine theorem gives a complete classification via a triple $(μ, σ², ν)$.",
    "whyMatters": []
  },
